01:01 Now it happened after the death of Moshe the servant of HaSHEM, that HaSHEM spoke to Yehoshua the son of Nun, Moshe' minister, saying,
01:02 Moshe my servant is dead; now therefore arise, go over this Yarden, you, and all this people, to the land which I do give to them, even to the children of Yisra'el.
01:03 Every place that the sole of your foot shall tread on, to you have I given it, as I spoke to Moshe.
01:04 From the wilderness, and this Levanon, even to the great river, the river Perat, all the land of the Chitti, and to the great sea toward the going down of the sun, shall be your border.
01:05 There shall not any man be able to stand before you all the days of your life. As I was with Moshe, so I will be with you; I will not fail you, nor forsake you.
01:06 Be strong and of good courage; for you shall cause this people to inherit the land which I swore to their fathers to give them.
01:07 Only be strong and very courageous, to observe to do according to all the law, which Moshe my servant commanded you: don't turn from it to the right hand or to the left, that you may have good success wherever you go.
01:08 This book of the law shall not depart out of your mouth, but you shall meditate thereon day and night, that you may observe to do according to all that is written therein: for then you shall make your way prosperous, and then you shall have good success.
01:09 Haven't I commanded you? Be strong and of good courage; don't be afraid, neither be dismayed: for HaSHEM your G-D is with you wherever you go.
01:10 Then Yehoshua commanded the officers of the people, saying,
01:11 Pass through the midst of the camp, and command the people, saying, Prepare you victuals; for within three days you are to pass over this Yarden, to go in to possess the land, which HaSHEM your G-D gives you to possess it.
01:12 To the Re'uveni, and to the Gadi, and to the half-tribe of Menashshe, spoke Yehoshua, saying,
01:13 Remember the word which Moshe the servant of HaSHEM commanded you, saying, HaSHEM your G-D gives you rest, and will give you this land.
01:14 Your wives, your little ones, and your cattle, shall abide in the land which Moshe gave you beyond the Yarden; but you shall pass over before your brothers armed, all the mighty men of valor, and shall help them;
01:15 until HaSHEM have given your brothers rest, as he has given you, and they also have possessed the land which HaSHEM your G-D gives them: then you shall return to the land of your possession, and possess it, which Moshe the servant of HaSHEM gave you beyond the Yarden toward the sunrise.
01:16 They answered Yehoshua, saying, All that you have commanded us we will do, and wherever you send us we will go.
01:17 According as we listened to Moshe in all things, so will we listen to you: only HaSHEM your G-D be with you, as he was with Moshe.
01:18 Whoever he be who shall rebel against your commandment, and shall not listen to your words in all that you command him, he shall be put to death: only be strong and of good courage.  
02:01 Yehoshua the son of Nun sent out of Shittim two men as spies secretly, saying, Go, view the land, and Yericho. They went and came into the house of a prostitute whose name was Rachav, and lay there.
02:02 It was told the king of Yericho, saying, Behold, there came men in here tonight of the children of Yisra'el to search out the land.
02:03 The king of Yericho sent to Rachav, saying, Bring forth the men who are come to you, who have entered into your house; for they have come to search out all the land.
02:04 The woman took the two men, and hid them; and she said, Yes, the men came to me, but I didn't know whence they were:
02:05 and it happened about the time of the shutting of the gate, when it was dark, that the men went out; where the men went I don't know: pursue after them quickly; for you will overtake them.
02:06 But she had brought them up to the roof, and hid them with the stalks of flax, which she had laid in order on the roof.
02:07 The men pursued after them the way to the Yarden to the fords: and as soon as those who pursued after them were gone out, they shut the gate.
02:08 Before they were laid down, she came up to them on the roof;
02:09 and she said to the men, I know that HaSHEM has given you the land, and that the fear of you is fallen on us, and that all the inhabitants of the land melt away before you.
02:10 For we have heard how HaSHEM dried up the water of the Sea of Suf before you, when you came out of Mitzrayim; and what you did to the two kings of the Amori, who were beyond the Yarden, to Sichon and to `Og, whom you utterly destroyed.
02:11 As soon as we had heard it, our hearts did melt, neither did there remain any more spirit in any man, because of you: for HaSHEM your G-D, he is G-D in Heaven above, and on earth beneath.
02:12 Now therefore, please swear to me by HaSHEM, since I have dealt kindly with you, that you also will deal kindly with my father's house, and give me a true token;
02:13 and that you will save alive my father, and my mother, and my brothers, and my sisters, and all that they have, and will deliver our lives from death.
02:14 The men said to her, Our life for yours, if you don't utter this our business; and it shall be, when HaSHEM gives us the land, that we will deal kindly and truly with you.
02:15 Then she let them down by a cord through the window: for her house was on the side of the wall, and she lived on the wall.
02:16 She said to them, Get you to the mountain, lest the pursuers light on you; and hide yourselves there three days, until the pursuers be returned: and afterward may you go your way.
02:17 The men said to her, We will be guiltless of this your oath which you have made us to swear.
02:18 Behold, when we come into the land, you shall bind this line of scarlet thread in the window which you did let us down by: and you shall gather to you into the house your father, and your mother, and your brothers, and all your father's household.
02:19 It shall be, that whoever shall go out of the doors of your house into the street, his blood shall be on his head, and we shall be guiltless: and whoever shall be with you in the house, his blood shall be on our head, if any hand be on him.
02:20 But if you utter this our business, then we shall be guiltless of your oath which you have made us to swear.
02:21 She said, According to your words, so be it. She sent them away, and they departed: and she bound the scarlet line in the window.
02:22 They went, and came to the mountain, and abode there three days, until the pursuers were returned: and the pursuers sought them throughout all the way, but didn't find them.
02:23 Then the two men returned, and descended from the mountain, and passed over, and came to Yehoshua the son of Nun; and they told him all that had befallen them.
02:24 They said to Yehoshua, Truly HaSHEM has delivered into our hands all the land; and moreover all the inhabitants of the land do melt away before us.  
03:01 Yehoshua rose up early in the morning; and they removed from Shittim, and came to the Yarden, he and all the children of Yisra'el; and they lodged there before they passed over.
03:02 It happened after three days, that the officers went through the midst of the camp;
03:03 and they commanded the people, saying, When you see the ark of the covenant of HaSHEM your G-D, and the Cohanim the Levites bearing it, then you shall remove from your place, and go after it.
03:04 Yet there shall be a space between you and it, about two thousand cubits by measure: don't come near to it, that you may know the way by which you must go; for you have not passed this way heretofore.
03:05 Yehoshua said to the people, Sanctify yourselves; for tomorrow HaSHEM will do wonders among you.
03:06 Yehoshua spoke to the Cohanim, saying, Take up the ark of the covenant, and pass over before the people. They took up the ark of the covenant, and went before the people.
03:07 HaSHEM said to Yehoshua, This day will I begin to magnify you in the sight of all Yisra'el, that they may know that, as I was with Moshe, so I will be with you.
03:08 You shall command the Cohanim who bear the ark of the covenant, saying, When you are come to the brink of the waters of the Yarden, you shall stand still in the Yarden.
03:09 Yehoshua said to the children of Yisra'el, Come here, and hear the words of HaSHEM your G-D.
03:10 Yehoshua said, Hereby you shall know that the living G-D is among you, and that he will without fail drive out from before you the Cana`ani, and the Chittite, and the Chivvi, and the Perizzi, and the Girgashi, and the Amori, and the Yevusi.
03:11 Behold, the ark of the covenant of the L-rd of all the earth passes over before you into the Yarden.
03:12 Now therefore take you twelve men out of the tribes of Yisra'el, for every tribe a man.
03:13 It shall come to pass, when the soles of the feet of the Cohanim who bear the ark of HaSHEM, the L-rd of all the earth, shall rest in the waters of the Yarden, that the waters of the Yarden shall be cut off, even the waters that come down from above; and they shall stand in one heap.
03:14 It happened, when the people removed from their tents, to pass over the Yarden, the Cohanim who bore the ark of the covenant being before the people;
03:15 and when those who bore the ark were come to the Yarden, and the feet of the Cohanim who bore the ark were dipped in the brink of the water (for the Yarden overflows all its banks all the time of harvest,)
03:16 that the waters which came down from above stood, and rose up in one heap, a great way off, at Adam, the city that is beside Tzaretan; and those that went down toward the sea of the `Aravah, even the Salt Sea, were wholly cut off: and the people passed over right against Yericho.
03:17 The Cohanim who bore the ark of the covenant of HaSHEM stood firm on dry ground in the midst of the Yarden; and all Yisra'el passed over on dry ground, until all the nation were passed clean over the Yarden.  
05:01 It happened, when all the kings of the Amori, who were beyond the Yarden westward, and all the kings of the Cana`anim, who were by the sea, heard how that HaSHEM had dried up the waters of the Yarden from before the children of Yisra'el, until we were passed over, that their heart melted, neither was there spirit in them any more, because of the children of Yisra'el.
05:02 At that time HaSHEM said to Yehoshua, Make you flint knives, and circumcise again the children of Yisra'el the second time.
05:03 Yehoshua made himself flint knives, and circumcised the children of Yisra'el at the hill of `Aralot.
05:04 This is the cause why Yehoshua did circumcise: all the people who came forth out of Mitzrayim, who were males, even all the men of war, died in the wilderness by the way, after they came forth out of Mitzrayim.
05:05 For all the people who came out were circumcised; but all the people who were born in the wilderness by the way as they came forth out of Mitzrayim, they had not circumcised.
05:06 For the children of Yisra'el walked forty years in the wilderness, until all the nation, even the men of war who came forth out of Mitzrayim, were consumed, because they didn't listen to the voice of HaSHEM: to whom HaSHEM swore that he wouldn't let them see the land which HaSHEM swore to their fathers that he would give us, a land flowing with milk and honey.
05:07 Their children, whom he raised up in their place, them did Yehoshua circumcise: for they were uncircumcised, because they had not circumcised them by the way.
05:08 It happened, when they had done circumcising all the nation, that they abode in their places in the camp, until they were whole.
05:09 HaSHEM said to Yehoshua, This day have I rolled away the reproach of Mitzrayim from off you. Therefore the name of that place was called Gilgal, to this day.
05:10 The children of Yisra'el encamped in Gilgal; and they kept the Pesach on the fourteenth day of the month at even in the plains of Yericho.
05:11 They ate of the produce of the land on the next day after the Pesach, unleavened cakes and parched grain, in the same day.
05:12 The manna ceased on the next day, after they had eaten of the produce of the land; neither had the children of Yisra'el manna any more; but they ate of the fruit of the land of Cana`an that year.
05:13 It happened, when Yehoshua was by Yericho, that he lifted up his eyes and looked, and, behold, there stood a man over against him with his sword drawn in his hand: and Yehoshua went to him, and said to him, Are you for us, or for our adversaries?
05:14 He said, No; but as prince of the host of HaSHEM am I now come. Yehoshua fell on his face to the earth, and did worship, and said to him, What says my lord to his servant?
05:15 The prince of HaSHEM's host said to Yehoshua, Put off your shoe from off your foot; for the place whereon you stand is holy. Yehoshua did so.  
06:01 Now Yericho was tightly shut up because of the children of Yisra'el: none went out, and none came in.
06:02 HaSHEM said to Yehoshua, Behold, I have given into your hand Yericho, and the king of it, and the mighty men of valor.
06:03 You shall compass the city, all the men of war, going about the city once. Thus shall you do six days.
06:04 Seven Cohanim shall bear seven shofarot of rams' horns before the ark: and the seventh day you shall compass the city seven times, and the Cohanim shall blow the shofarot.
06:05 It shall be that when they make a long blast with the ram's horn, and when you hear the sound of the shofar, all the people shall shout with a great shout; and the wall of the city shall fall down flat, and the people shall go up every man straight before him.
06:06 Yehoshua the son of Nun called the Cohanim, and said to them, Take up the ark of the covenant, and let seven Cohanim bear seven shofarot of rams' horns before the ark of HaSHEM.
06:07 They said to the people, Pass on, and compass the city, and let the armed men pass on before the ark of HaSHEM.
06:08 It was so, that when Yehoshua had spoken to the people, the seven Cohanim bearing the seven shofarot of rams' horns before HaSHEM passed on, and blew the shofarot: and the ark of the covenant of HaSHEM followed them.
06:09 The armed men went before the Cohanim who blew the shofarot, and the rearward went after the ark, the Cohanim blowing the shofarot as they went.
06:10 Yehoshua commanded the people, saying, You shall not shout, nor let your voice be heard, neither shall any word proceed out of your mouth, until the day I bid you shout; then shall you shout.
06:11 So he caused the ark of HaSHEM to compass the city, going about it once: and they came into the camp, and lodged in the camp.
06:12 Yehoshua rose early in the morning, and the Cohanim took up the ark of HaSHEM.
06:13 The seven Cohanim bearing the seven shofarot of rams' horns before the ark of HaSHEM went on continually, and blew the shofarot: and the armed men went before them; and the rearward came after the ark of HaSHEM, the Cohanim blowing the shofarot as they went.
06:14 The second day they compassed the city once, and returned into the camp: so they did six days.
06:15 It happened on the seventh day, that they rose early at the dawning of the day, and compassed the city after the same manner seven times: only on the day they compassed the city seven times.
06:16 It happened at the seventh time, when the Cohanim blew the shofarot, Yehoshua said to the people, Shout; for HaSHEM has given you the city.
06:17 The city shall be devoted, even it and all that is therein, to HaSHEM: only Rachav the prostitute shall live, she and all who are with her in the house, because she hid the messengers that we sent.
06:18 But as for you, only keep yourselves from the devoted thing, lest when you have devoted it, you take of the devoted thing; so would you make the camp of Yisra'el accursed, and trouble it.
06:19 But all the silver, and gold, and vessels of brass and iron, are holy to HaSHEM: they shall come into the treasury of HaSHEM.
06:20 So the people shouted, and the Cohanim blew the shofarot; and it happened, when the people heard the sound of the shofar, that the people shouted with a great shout, and the wall fell down flat, so that the people went up into the city, every man straight before him, and they took the city.
06:21 They utterly destroyed all that was in the city, both man and woman, both young and old, and ox, and sheep, and donkey, with the edge of the sword.
06:22 Yehoshua said to the two men who had spied out the land, Go into the prostitute's house, and bring out there the woman, and all that she has, as you swore to her.
06:23 The young men the spies went in, and brought out Rachav, and her father, and her mother, and her brothers, and all that she had; all her relatives also they brought out; and they set them outside of the camp of Yisra'el.
06:24 They burnt the city with fire, and all that was therein; only the silver, and the gold, and the vessels of brass and of iron, they put into the treasury of the house of HaSHEM.
06:25 But Rachav the prostitute, and her father's household, and all that she had, did Yehoshua save alive; and she lived in the midst of Yisra'el to this day, because she hid the messengers, whom Yehoshua sent to spy out Yericho.
06:26 Yehoshua charged them with an oath at that time, saying, Cursed be the man before HaSHEM, that rises up and builds this city Yericho: with the loss of his firstborn shall he lay the foundation of it, and with the loss of his youngest son shall he set up the gates of it.
06:27 So HaSHEM was with Yehoshua; and his fame was in all the land.  
